# %% [markdown]
# # specs_novel — Phase 3: decoder training (Colab, GPU)
#
# `specs_novel/roadmap.md` P3. Every value here is pre-registered in `specs_novel/gate_report.md` →
# **G3** (design: `specs_novel/phase3_plan.md` §4–§5). **Generated by `build/mk_novel_p0.py` — do not
# hand-edit.**
#
# Runtime: **A100 or L4**. One epoch is ≈ 715 steps at batch 256 *molecules*, so epochs are minutes,
# not tens of minutes. Budget for P3 is ~50–60 compute units; the calibration cell projects the run
# before it starts.
#
# | step | what |
# |---|---|
# | structures | every corpus ik14 → prep, SELFIES ids, **oracle formula** (RDKit, H included), `in_scope`; cached on Drive |
# | index | `dec_split == "train"` ∩ in scope ∩ ≥ 1 quality-OK row → flat arrays; `dec_val` likewise |
# | model | `DreamsSelfiesDecoder`, `D_MODEL` 512, 8 layers, 8 heads, tied embeddings (≈ 28 M params) |
# | training | teacher forcing, ≤ 4 spectra per molecule per epoch, **CE dropout 0.3**, bf16 |
# | early stop | patience **5** on `dec_val` token CE — this is G3.2 |
#
# **Resumability.** Every epoch writes the model, optimizer, scheduler, epoch, patience **and all
# four RNG states** to Drive, atomically. If Colab disconnects, just re-run this notebook top to
# bottom: it prints `resumed from epoch N` and continues. Without the RNG state a resumed run would
# silently train on a different sampling stream, which would make the epoch count and G3.2
# meaningless.
#
# Outputs go to Drive `casmi_2026/_novel/p3/`: `structures.parquet`, `index_train.npz`,
# `index_dec_val.npz`, `ckpt/epoch_*.pt`, `decoder.pt`, `train_log.jsonl`. Paste the final printout
# back into the chat.

